ce_id": "step_16", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "1006 fires only 3 times in the window; the only structural route to 1860 is 1006->1680->153->1860 (1860 is not even within 2 hops of 1006). That 3-hop path allows a maximum span of 2x600=1200 units, but the single 153->1860 contact falls in [43531,44431] while 1006's last usable event is at or before 41731 (and the 1006->1680 event is either ~36k, far too early, or ~47k, after 1860 goes silent). Static connectivity, hub activity of 153, and overall event volume exist but do not yield a time-respecting <=600-unit chain."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structure (time-ignored):** 1006's entire 1-hop set is {1075, 1532, 1680}, and 1860 does not appear anywhere in 1006's 2-hop neighbourhood (step_03). The only feasible route is 1006 \u2192 1680 \u2192 153 \u2192 1860 (153 is the only in-neighbour of 1860 that appears in 1006's neighbourhood at all; step_04).\n\n**Timing:**\n- 1006 has only 3 events in the whole window (step_02): one in [35431,37231], one in [41281,41731], one in [46231,48031] (steps 05, 11, 14).\n- The 1006\u21921680 event is *not* the [41281,41731] one (step_15), so it sits at ~36k or ~47k (step_12).\n- The single 153\u21921860 contact is bracketed to [43531, 44431] (steps 09, 10, 13).\n\n**Feasibility check:** the 3-hop path 1006\u21921680\u2192153\u21921860 has only two inter-event gaps, so it can span at most 2\u00d7600 = 1200 time units. From 1006's latest pre-target event (\u226441731) to the 153\u21921860 event (\u226543531) the span is \u22651800 \u2014 too long. If 1006\u21921680 fired at ~36k, the gap is \u22656300; if it fired at ~47k it is *after* 1860's last event entirely (1860 is silent after 44431, step_06). No admissible \u2264600-unit chain exists.\n\n**Confounders ruled out:** the window holds 5134 events over 1863 nodes (step_01) and 153 is a hub firing 15 times in [41731,44431] (step_16) \u2014 high volume and hub popularity, plus static reachability (step_03), but none of these produce a valid time-respecting chain.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_378e517f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860, 1680, 153],\n  \"window\": [22831, 51631],\n  \"confidence\": 0.76,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1006 fires only 3 times in the window; the only structural route to 1860 is 1006->1680->153->1860 (1860 is not even within 2 hops of 1006). That 3-hop path allows a maximum span of 2x600=1200 units, but the single 153->1860 contact falls in [43531,44431] while 1006's last usable event is at or before 41731 (and the 1006->1680 event is either ~36k, far too early, or ~47k, after 1860 goes silent). Static connectivity, hub activity of 153, and overall event volume exist but do not yield a time-respecting <=600-unit chain.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 44774, "total_output_tokens": 8741, "total_tokens": 53515, "total_latency_ms": 111561, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}